.TH DANBY-PERIODICVOLTERRA 1
.SH NAME
danby-periodicvolterra \- predator and prey with a periodic birthrate
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/periodicvolterra
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Periodicvolterra
shows how seasonal variation changes the closed orbits of the Volterra model.
.SH MODEL
X' = a(1+s cos(wt))X-bXY;
Y' = cXY-dY.
.PP
X and Y are prey and predator populations.  The controls set mean prey birth
a, predation b, conversion c, predator death d, seasonal amplitude s, and
angular frequency w.  Setting s to zero recovers the autonomous Volterra
model.  The marked point (d/c,a/b) is the equilibrium of that mean model;
with seasonal forcing it is a reference point rather than a fixed solution.
.SH DISPLAY
The left panel is the population phase portrait.  The right panel plots both
populations against time, so forcing, phase lag, and modulation are visible.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag the phase portrait to choose the two initial populations.  Drag the six
bottom tracks to alter the parameters.  Space pauses, period advances one
display step, r resets, and q or Escape exits.
.SH NUMERICS
The model is implemented separately in
.B /appl/danby/periodicvolterra.b
and integrated with the general-purpose fourth-order Runge-Kutta routine in
.IR numerics (2).
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/periodicvolterra.b
.br
.B /appl/temple/ecology.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR danby-ecology (1),
.IR numerics (2)
